From edd3a48463d29f3f20d3d8748d3f591bcc26e267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/exynos: add Exynos 9820 DisplayPort controller and DECON2
 KMS drivers

External display over USB-C DisplayPort alternate mode on the Exynos
9820, with the bindings of both devices:

 - exynos9820_dp: DisplayPort transmitter as a DRM bridge. AUX
   channel, link training with rate fallback on top of the combo PHY's
   DP mode, SST video timing from the display mode, HPD handling as a
   Type-C mux/orientation switch, lane direction from the USB/DP
   select GPIO or the Type-C orientation.
 - exynos9820_decon2: KMS driver for DECON2, the display controller of
   the DP output. Cold init modelled on the vendor decon/dpp code
   (DECON0's takeover driver is not touched): one full-screen primary
   plane on window 4 / IDMA GF1 with XRGB/ARGB/XBGR/ABGR8888, shadow
   updates latched at frame start, vblank from the frame start
   interrupt. The window registers live in DECON0's register block,
   which is mapped without claiming it; the probe refuses if DECON0
   uses the same window, channel or SRAM banks. Separate DRM device
   with a bridge connector (EDID/HPD from the DP bridge), mode limits
   max_width/max_height/max_clock_khz (default 1920x1200, 165 MHz),
   optional fbdev. The driver only binds with enable=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
